---
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
import Header from '../components/Header.astro'
import { DOCS } from '../data/site'
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'

const CONTACT = 'privacy@tiko.run'
---

<Base title="Privacy · tiko" description="What tiko.run keeps when you join the tiko Cloud waitlist, where it is kept and how to have it removed.">
  <Header />
  <main id="main" class="wrap">
    <article>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="meta">Updated October 17, 2026</p>

      <p>
        This page covers the tiko.run website. It sets no cookies of its own and runs no analytics or ad
        trackers. The only thing it keeps is your e-mail address, and only if you give it to us in the
        tiko Cloud form.
      </p>

      <h2>The tiko Cloud waitlist</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>What we keep</dt>
        <dd>Your e-mail address, the time you sent it, which form you used, whether you ticked news and updates, and the country your request came from. Not your IP address.</dd>
        <dt>Why</dt>
        <dd>To send you one e-mail when tiko Cloud opens. If you ticked news, that e-mail asks you to confirm it, and only after you confirm do we write now and then about what is new in tiko. No spam, and the address is never shared or sold.</dd>
        <dt>Where</dt>
        <dd>In a Postgres database run by Neon in the EU (Frankfurt). The form sends it through a Cloudflare Worker, which can add addresses but not read them back.</dd>
        <dt>Bot check</dt>
        <dd>The form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to tell people from bots. It loads only when you use the form. Cloudflare's own <a class="link" href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/">Turnstile privacy addendum</a> applies to it.</dd>
        <dt>How long</dt>
        <dd>Until we have sent the e-mail about Cloud opening, then the address is deleted, unless you confirmed news from it. Then until you unsubscribe, which every e-mail lets you do in one click.</dd>
        <dt>Removal</dt>
        <dd>Write to <a class="link" href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a> from that address, and we delete it. The same address can ask what we keep about it.</dd>
      </dl>

      <h2>tiko itself</h2>
      <p>
        tiko runs on your own server and keeps your data there. What a running tiko sends, and how to
        turn it off, is listed in <a class="link" href={`${DOCS}/privacy/`}>Usage stats</a> in the guide.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  article {
    max-width: 44rem;
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }
  .meta {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }
  h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  dl {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 9rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }
  dt {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  dd {
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    dl {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0.25rem;
    }
    dd + dt {
      margin-top: 0.75rem;
    }
  }
</style>
